    {
      "slug": "acs",
      "name": "ACS",
      "category": "technology",
      "model": "",
      "specs": [],
      "images": [
        {
          "src": "img/products/acs/01.jpg",
          "text": "The ACS (AGV Control System) is monitoring the AGV system, which is operated in the background. The ACS controls the whole AGV system. It handles transport orders, allocates vehicles, and selects routes for the different transport assignments. It also controls the traffic flow. Efficient transportation is achieved by optimizing vehicle allocation and route planning for each assignment. Transport orders are generated through digital I/O or via interface, or communication with a host of MES. Through blockings in the system layout, the ACS prevents collisions not only between vehicles but also between vehicles and objects (e.g. doors, machines, etc). The ACS has a function to interface for handling sensors, push buttons, doors, etc."
        }
      ],
      "source": "https://www.agvsk.com/bbs/content.php?co_id=acs"
    },
    {
      "slug": "system-design-tools",
      "name": "System Design Tools",
      "category": "technology",
      "model": "",
      "specs": [],
      "images": [
        {
          "src": "img/products/tools/01.jpg",
          "text": "The Traffic Tool has a lot of functions to control the traffic zones and segments. An operator or a manager is able to set all kinds of traffic zones with the tool even though there are various difficult traffics. It is easy and simple for the operator to control the Traffic tool like clicking. And, if there are some mistakes about setting many segments, the Traffic Tool will be indicated what mistake is located in. Also, the Traffic Tool can immediately show the optimal path(way) of AGV."
        },
        {
          "src": "img/products/tools/02.jpg",
          "text": "The layout(drawing) of other companies might be bitmap style. However, AGVS has the different style(vector type). The AGV Mapmaker can export the layout as vector method to show it on ACS(monitoring program)."
        }
      ],
      "source": "https://www.agvsk.com/bbs/content.php?co_id=tools"
